    <DataNode elementId="AT3G25900-MONOMER" textLabel="Homocysteine S-methyltransferase 1" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q9SDL7" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="275" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">NIL There are two homocysteine methyltransferases in Arabidopsis, AtHMT-1 and AtHMT-2. The specific activity of AtHMT-1 is about 10-fold higher than that of AtHMT-2. Both utilize S-methylmethionine and S-adenosylmethionine as methyl donors, and have higher affinities with S-methylmethionine. AtHMT-1 is strongly inhibited by methionine, whereas AtHMT-2 is not.</Comment>
